# Product documentation

Markdown in this repo is **product description**, not a developer handbook.

When you ship, change, or remove user-facing behavior (learning loop, identity, scoring, puzzle, credentials, honesty language, or trust model), update the relevant `.md` files in the same change.

## What docs are for

- What SkillForge is and who it is for
- The learner loop (learn → challenge → earn → unlock → forge → prove)
- What is shipped versus planned
- Claimed vs issuer-attested credentials (never blur them)
- Account vs optional wallet
- XP, paths, tracks, streaks, puzzle, and leaderboard as product behavior

## What docs must not include

- Install, env, deploy, CI, or test commands
- File trees, npm scripts, or operator runbooks
- Setup guides, RPC URLs, or “how to run locally”

## Files

- `README.md` — product overview
- `docs/STATUS.md` — current shipped state
- `docs/ROADMAP.md` — phases and remaining work
- `docs/PROGRESSION.md` — learning and gamification model
- `docs/CREDENTIAL.md` — credential product model
- `docs/AUTHORIZATION.md` — issuer attestation as a trust product
- `docs/METADATA.md` — what the on-chain certificate record shows

Keep names, honesty copy, and Fuji-live facts consistent across these files.
